      "ruleId": "built-in:code",
      "aspect": "correctness",
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "Fixed detail column can collapse the table on narrow viewports",
      "description": "When \u0060.has-detail\u0060 is active, the grid always reserves 350px for the detail pane. On a phone-sized viewport, the remaining \u0060minmax(0,1fr)\u0060 track can shrink to nearly zero, leaving the primary coverage table effectively unusable. The fixed 240px sticky boundary column further increases the minimum useful table width.",
      "recommendation": "Add a responsive breakpoint that stacks the detail pane, turns it into an overlay, or replaces the fixed width with a bounded responsive track such as \u0060minmax(260px, 35vw)\u0060. Verify both table and detail interactions at narrow viewport widths.",
